rsx fp decompiler: texel (UNNORM) coordinates of a 3D texture are divided by its depth too.

rsx_fp_apply_unnorm_scale appended " * float2(1/w, 1/h)" to every Sample of an unnormalised unit. A volume unit is
declared Texture3D and sampled with a float3, so the result did not compile ("'__BI_Sample' : no matching overloaded
function found") and the pipeline was dropped. Resistance 3's SSAO pass samples a 32x32x32 volume that way: with the
pass dropped, the AO filter after it read the leftover shadow-map bytes at the same address (0x1DA8800) as its input,
and the Home level's walls, floor and props came out almost black (mean frame brightness 7/255 against about 24 on
the console). A volume unit now gets float3(1/w, 1/h, 1/depth), as RPCS3's
texture cache scales a 3D texture's r by 1/depth; the engine passes its volume mask and the depth, live_draw (no 3D
textures) passes an empty mask.

test_shader_msl: a TEX on an unnormalised 3D unit gets the float3 scale and translates to MSL.
Scripted run (Home level, CHAPTER ONE view): mean brightness 7 -> 19, walls and floor lit as on the console.

Upstream: PR #482.
